commit 53a5d17947e991a9addec4e5cf0af7fc5cffaea5
Author: haileen7 <haileen7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 20:58:49 2026 +0000

    fix(hardware-audit): write the audit row only after a successful UPDATE (#1279)
    
    The observer wrote the `updated` audit row from the `updating` hook, i.e.
    before the UPDATE ran. An aborted save (a later `updating` listener throwing),
    a cancelled save, or an exception swallowed inside a committed transaction left
    a phantom audit row describing a change that never landed.
    
    `updated` fires after a successful UPDATE and before `syncOriginal()`, so
    `getChanges()` holds this save's attributes and `getOriginal()` the previous
    values — same diff, written only when the write happened. AUDITED_FIELDS ⊆
    fillable is pinned by a contract test.
commit 53a5d17947e991a9addec4e5cf0af7fc5cffaea5
Author: haileen7 <haileen7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 20:58:49 2026 +0000

    fix(hardware-audit): write the audit row only after a successful UPDATE (#1279)
    
    The observer wrote the `updated` audit row from the `updating` hook, i.e.
    before the UPDATE ran. An aborted save (a later `updating` listener throwing),
    a cancelled save, or an exception swallowed inside a committed transaction left
    a phantom audit row describing a change that never landed.
    
    `updated` fires after a successful UPDATE and before `syncOriginal()`, so
    `getChanges()` holds this save's attributes and `getOriginal()` the previous
    values — same diff, written only when the write happened. AUDITED_FIELDS ⊆
    fillable is pinned by a contract test.
    
    Known trade-off (R1): a failing audit INSERT after a successful UPDATE leaves
    the data change unlogged; fixing that needs a transaction at every call site.

diff --git a/app/Observers/HardwareAuditObserver.php b/app/Observers/HardwareAuditObserver.php
index 6c1e1fd0..3ed57139 100644
--- a/app/Observers/HardwareAuditObserver.php
+++ b/app/Observers/HardwareAuditObserver.php
@@ -49,10 +49,17 @@ public function created(Hardware $hardware): void
     /**
      * Handle the Hardware "updated" event.
      *
-     * We use `updating` (fires BEFORE the model syncs its changes)
-     * because in `updated` the dirty attributes are already cleared.
+     * `updated` fires from `performUpdate()` after the UPDATE has succeeded and
+     * before `syncOriginal()`, so `getChanges()` holds this save's attributes
+     * and `getOriginal()` still holds the previous values. Using `updating`
+     * wrote the audit row before the UPDATE, leaving a phantom row whenever the
+     * save was aborted or failed.
+     *
+     * Known trade-off (R1): if the audit INSERT itself fails after a successful
+     * UPDATE, the data change persists without an audit row. Fixing that needs
+     * a transaction at every call site — out of scope for #1279.
      */
-    public function updating(Hardware $hardware): void
+    public function updated(Hardware $hardware): void
     {
         if ($this->shouldSuppress()) {
             return;
@@ -185,7 +192,7 @@ protected function sanitizeChanges(?array $changes): ?array
      */
     protected function getChangedFields(Hardware $hardware): array
     {
-        $dirty = $hardware->getDirty();
+        $dirty = $hardware->getChanges();
         $original = $hardware->getOriginal();
 
         $changes = [];
